    followUp: "Medical oncology in 4 weeks for chemotherapy initiation (if planned). PSA at 1 month (should drop significantly). Ongoing: ADT injections every 3 months. Monitor for castration-resistant progression (rising PSA despite castrate testosterone levels).",
    pearls: "ADT is the backbone of mHSPC treatment — prostate cancer cells are driven by androgens. The addition of Docetaxel chemotherapy to ADT improves overall survival by 13-15 months in high-volume disease (CHAARTED trial). Abiraterone + Prednisolone is an alternative for those unfit for chemo. GnRH agonists cause an initial testosterone surge (\"tumour flare\") — antiandrogen (Bicalutamide) for 2 weeks prevents this. GnRH antagonists (Degarelix) avoid the flare but are injectable monthly. Denosumab is superior to Zoledronic acid for preventing skeletal-related events.",
