    ddx: ["Colon Cancer Stage III", "Rectal Cancer", "Colonic Adenoma", "IBD-Associated Dysplasia"],
    goals: "Reduce risk of recurrence with adjuvant chemotherapy, manage treatment side effects, monitor for disease recurrence",
    pharm: "1. Adjuvant chemotherapy: FOLFOX regimen (Oxaliplatin 85mg/m2 IV Day 1 + Leucovorin 400mg/m2 IV Day 1 + 5-FU 400mg/m2 IV bolus then 2400mg/m2 IV infusion over 46 hours) every 2 weeks for 12 cycles (6 months). 2. Alternative: CAPOX regimen (Capecitabine 1000mg/m2 PO BID Days 1-14 + Oxaliplatin 130mg/m2 IV Day 1) every 3 weeks for 8 cycles. 3. If age >70: discuss risks/benefits of adding Oxaliplatin. 4. If MSI-H: consider single-agent immune checkpoint inhibitor (Pembrolizumab) instead of chemotherapy — not applicable here (MSS). 5. CEA monitoring every 3 months for 3 years. 6. Colonoscopy in 1 year.",
    nonPharm: "Dietary: small frequent meals, avoid cold foods (Oxaliplatin can cause pharyngolaryngeal dysaesthesia with cold). Exercise during treatment to reduce fatigue. Good oral hygiene. Hand-foot syndrome care (moisturisers, avoid hot water) if on Capecitabine.",
    carePlan: "Start adjuvant FOLFOX chemotherapy 4-8 weeks post-surgery. Place central line (PICC or Port-a-cath) for 5-FU infusion. Pre-medication: antiemetics (Aprepitant, Dexamethasone, 5-HT3 antagonist). Monitor for Oxaliplatin neurotoxicity at each cycle. Dose reduction or discontinuation if significant neuropathy.",
    dtps: "1. Stage III colon cancer with high risk of recurrence requiring adjuvant systemic therapy. 2. Chemotherapy toxicity management (neuropathy, neutropenia, fatigue, GI).",
    monitoring: "FBC before each cycle (ANC >1500). LFTs, Cr before each cycle. Neurotoxicity assessment (sensory, motor, functional). Monitor for: neutropenic fever, diarrhoea, stomatitis, hand-foot syndrome. CEA every 3 months. CT chest/abdomen/pelvis every 6-12 months for 3-5 years.",
    counselling: "Adjuvant chemotherapy reduces the risk of cancer returning by 30-50%. Treatment is given every 2 weeks for 6 months. The most notable side effect is nerve tingling/numbness from Oxaliplatin — avoid cold drinks and cold air during and after infusion. Most side effects are temporary. Stay active and eat well to maintain strength during treatment.",
    followUp: "Medical oncology every 2 cycles during treatment. CEA every 3 months. Colonoscopy in 1 year. CT scans every 6-12 months. Long-term: surveillance for 5 years, then less frequent.",
    pearls: "Adjuvant chemotherapy for Stage III colon cancer is standard of care — reduces 5-year recurrence risk from ~50% to ~25%. The MOSAIC trial established FOLFOX as the standard regimen. The addition of Oxaliplatin to 5-FU/Leucovorin improves disease-free survival by 7-8%. Cumulative Oxaliplatin-induced peripheral neuropathy is dose-limiting — assess before each cycle. Patients with MSI-H (15% of Stage III) may not benefit from 5-FU but benefit from immunotherapy.",
    references: ["NCCN Guidelines: Colon Cancer", "ESMO Guidelines: Colorectal Cancer", "Kenya Cancer Treatment Guidelines"],
